<title>MEXICO: Mexico mortgage needs $40 bln per year - industry.</title>
<headline>Mexico mortgage needs $40 bln per year - industry.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico needs investment of up to $40 billion per year in mortgages to satisfy the population's housing needs, a housing industry spokesman said.</p>
<p>&quot;We should be investing between $35 billion and $40 billion per year in mortgages ... to satisfy demand,&quot; said Jose Manuel Agudo,&quot; president of the Mexican Housing Promotors' Federation, at a ceremony to sign an agreement between banks and construction firms to promote housing and real estate development.</p>
<p>Agudo said between five million and eight million square meters (54-86 million square feet) of living space were built per year in Mexico.</p>
<p>Nonetheless, Agudo estimated 30 million square meters (320 million square feet) of living space per year were needed to satisfy new demand and alleviate existing backlog.</p>
<p>((--Cyntia Barrera, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9549))</p>
